OL,3,GNEWSATfL photocard breach exposes      
OL,4,A265,000 customers                      
OL,6,FThe personal details of about 265,000  
OL,7,FOyster photocard customers have been   
OL,8,Faccessed in a cyber breach, Transport  
OL,9,Ffor London (TfL) has said.             
OL,11,FNames, email and home addresses, phone 
OL,12,Fnumbers, dates of birth and security   
OL,13,Fquestions and answers were compromised 
OL,14,Fafter "suspicious activity" was        
OL,15,Fdetected on the photocard website on   
OL,16,FMonday.                                
OL,18,FTfL said it took the photocard system  
OL,19,Foffline to limit access and had        
OL,20,Fnotified the Information Commissioner's
OL,21,FOffice (ICO).                          
OL,23,APub: 18-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
